// Latency by endpoint: p50, p95, p99, and the error rate beside them.
//
// p50 and p99 together, never p50 alone or an average. A mean hides the tail
// entirely - one 9-second request among a hundred 50ms ones moves the average
// by 90ms and moves p99 to 9 seconds, and it is the second number that
// describes what a user actually hit. p95 is included as the middle sighting:
// when p95 is healthy and p99 is not, the problem is a small, specific set of
// requests (one slow query plan, one large tenant) rather than general load.
//
// Grouped by cloud_RoleName as well as operation_Name because this App
// Insights receives telemetry from three processes (QuotesApi, Quotes.Outbox,
// Quotes.Worker). Without the role, an endpoint's numbers could silently
// include another service's identically-named operation.
requests
| where timestamp > ago(1h)
| summarize
    calls      = count(),
    failures   = countif(success == false),
    p50        = percentile(duration, 50),
    p95        = percentile(duration, 95),
    p99        = percentile(duration, 99),
    maxMs      = max(duration)
  by cloud_RoleName, operation_Name
// round() because a p99 quoted to nine decimal places implies a precision
// that a percentile over a few hundred samples does not have.
| extend errorRatePct = round(100.0 * failures / calls, 2)
| project cloud_RoleName, operation_Name, calls, errorRatePct,
          p50 = round(p50, 1), p95 = round(p95, 1), p99 = round(p99, 1), maxMs = round(maxMs, 1)
| order by p99 desc
